abstract: We construct decomposition and occupation operators on a generated correlation-spectral
  arithmetic system. Prime residue classes form the augmentation cotangent basis, and the corresponding
  one-word vectors span the degree-one kernel of a decomposition Hodge Laplacian. The complementary
  spectral gap is exactly one, giving sharp heat and resolvent approximations to the prime projection
  and summable Gaussian trace errors. Symmetric and exterior occupations retain logarithmic
  arithmetic energy and quadratic correlation energy on the same value space. A faithful extension
  of addition records relative inputs; its charge defect intertwines input multiplicative parity
  with the parity of the sum. Common-factor coordinates and exact square-divisor identities
  give scale transforms of the resulting signed responses. Combining additive and decomposition
  responses defines a Gaussian endpoint map. Under diagonal self-consistency, this map has a
  unique stable fixed point with an enclosure of the complete infinite response. For compact
  Laplace realizations of square energy and quadratic shell capacity, Weyl counting gives dimension
  three; further geometric and central-sign classifications hold in their stated realization
  classes. Counting applications recover Bertrand's theorem, the prime-number asymptotic and
  square-free sign densities through the occupation traces and their boundary responses.
